# Feature-based architecture

Organize all new and moved Dart/Flutter code by **feature**, not by technical type at `lib/` root.

## Top-level layout

```text
lib/
  main.dart              # bootstrap only (runApp, ProviderScope if used)
  app/                   # app shell: theme, router, global providers
  core/                  # cross-feature only (no feature-specific logic)
  features/
    <feature_name>/      # one folder per user-facing capability
```

## Per-feature structure

Each feature is self-contained. Use layers that fit the feature size; skip empty layers:

```text
lib/features/<feature_name>/
  presentation/   # pages, widgets, Riverpod notifiers/providers
  domain/         # entities, repository interfaces (optional for tiny features)
  data/           # models, repository implementations, API/local sources
```

Folder names: `snake_case` (e.g. `lecture_viewer`, `translation_session`).

## Where code belongs

| Location | Put here |
|----------|----------|
| `lib/features/<feature>/` | UI, state, repos, models used by one feature |
| `lib/core/` | extensions, failures, shared widgets, constants used by 2+ features |
| `lib/app/` | `MaterialApp`, routes, theme, app-wide DI setup |
| `lib/` root | **Only** `main.dart` — not `widgets/`, `services/`, `models/` |

**Imports:** Features may depend on `core` and `app`. Features must **not** import another feature's `data/` or `presentation/` directly — move shared contracts to `core` or a thin shared module.

## When adding or moving code

- New screen or flow → folder under `lib/features/<name>/`
- New file → correct layer (`presentation` / `domain` / `data`), not beside `main.dart`
- Growing `main.dart` → extract to `app/` and feature folders
- Tests mirror features: `test/features/<feature_name>/...`

## Import examples

```dart
// Good
import 'package:lecture_viewer_v3/features/lectures/presentation/lecture_list_page.dart';

// Bad — feature UI at lib root
import 'package:lecture_viewer_v3/lecture_list_page.dart';
```
